# BOM standard (RAD)

When creating or editing any `hardware/<product>/bom.csv`, follow the canonical
RAD BOM standard.

Full reference: https://dev.researchanddesire.com/meta/bom-standard/

The vendored schema lives at `.github/workflows/scripts/bom.schema.json`; do not
hand-edit it.

## Header

```csv
#,Part Name,Category,Description,Qty,UOM,Manufacturer,MFG PN,Vendor,Vendor PN,Source,Notes
```

## Conventions

- Use the header exactly, in the same order.
- Use only canonical category codes from the standard.
- Use an en dash `–` for empty values; do not leave blank cells.
- `Qty` must parse as a number.
- `Source` should prefer an in-repo source path when one exists.

Run `python .github/workflows/scripts/bom_lint.py` after edits.
